      "role": "user",
      "content": "Wait, it looks like the response cut off mid-sentence. Can you finish that and give me the full list of 5? \n\nAlso, looking at the ones you did start, they feel a bit... generic? Like, standard HR stuff. I'm worried they might not be hitting our specific company culture hard enough. If you can, try to weave in the rest of our core values more explicitly so the metric reflects our specific culture—but again, please don't make it weird. I don't want the candidate to feel like they're being interrogated by a buzzword generator. Just make sure they actually reflect those themes like synergy and growth-mindset.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here are the five behavioral interview questions, with a focus on explicitly incorporating your company's core values and avoiding generic, buzzword-heavy language:\n\n1. Can you describe a project where you identified a process inefficiency and proposed an innovative solution that improved team productivity? How did you ensure your idea was feasible and aligned with the team's goals, and what specific synergies did you identify between different departments or functions?\n\n(This question tests the candidate's ability to think creatively and propose solutions that benefit the team, while also demonstrating their understanding of collaboration and teamwork.)\n\n2. Tell me about a time when you had to adapt your approach to a complex problem that required input from multiple stakeholders. How did you facilitate open communication and ensure everyone's perspectives were considered, and what did you learn about the importance of growth-mindset in driving innovation?\n\n(This question assesses the candidate's ability to collaborate with diverse stakeholders, think on their feet, and prioritize effective communication, while also highlighting the importance of growth-mindset in driving innovation.)\n\n3. Describe a situation where you were part of a cross-functional team working on a high-priority project. How did you contribute to the team's efforts, and what innovative ideas did you bring to the table that helped drive growth",
